# G15 — the source coefficient: the literal Weil normalization, and the verdict of the gate

**The Riemann Hypothesis is not proved.**  Nothing was weakened and nothing was
assumed: `RiemannHypothesisFor`, `RiemannHypothesis`, `CompletedRiemannHypothesis`
and every earlier statement are untouched; there is no `sorry`/`admit`, no
`axiom`, no postulate, no Boolean receipt, no numerical evidence and no
`@[implemented_by]` in any Lean source of this cycle.  `lake build
RiemannAnalytic` succeeds (8099 jobs) and `#print axioms` on every new theorem
returns only `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`.

The instruction for this cycle was: *stop doing abstract prime-distribution work,
and resolve the literal source coefficient — compute `C_src` and decide the gate
green / amber / red.*  This report states exactly what was decided, exactly what
was proved, and exactly what remains open.

